(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'READING','Comprehension – Literal',1,
'Artificial intelligence, or AI, refers to computer systems designed to perform tasks that would normally require human intelligence. Modern AI can recognise speech, translate languages, recommend music and films, detect diseases in medical images, and even write text. Machine learning, a branch of AI, enables computers to improve their performance over time by analysing large amounts of data. AI is already embedded in many everyday technologies, from the navigation apps on our phones to the filters that detect spam in our emails. As AI capabilities continue to advance, some economists predict significant disruption to the job market, with automation replacing certain routine tasks. However, many experts argue that AI will also create new types of employment and increase productivity across industries.','TEXT',
