'Which sentence contains a correctly placed participial phrase?','{"A":"Running to catch the bus, the rain started.","B":"Running to catch the bus, she slipped on the wet path.","C":"She slipped on the wet path, running to catch the bus.","D":"Running, the wet path caused her to slip."}','{"value":"B"}','The participial phrase "Running to catch the bus" must be followed immediately by the subject doing the running: "she".','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),

-- ADVANCED / MEDIUM
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Rhetorical Devices',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which device is used in: "The government''s response was as swift as a glacier moving uphill"?','{"A":"Metaphor","B":"Personification","C":"Ironic simile","D":"Hyperbole"}','{"value":"C"}','The simile compares the response to a glacier moving uphill (an impossibility), making it ironic — implying the government was very slow.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Clauses',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence contains an appositive phrase?','{"A":"She studied hard before the exam.","B":"Charles Darwin, the father of evolutionary theory, changed science forever.","C":"Darwin, who was born in 1809, studied medicine first.","D":"Darwin studied biology and medicine."}','{"value":"B"}','An appositive is a noun phrase that renames or identifies the noun beside it: "the father of evolutionary theory" renames Darwin.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Vocabulary',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which word best completes the sentence: "The documentary presented a ___ argument for reforming the justice system."','{"A":"cogent","B":"vague","C":"flimsy","D":"peripheral"}','{"value":"A"}','"Cogent" means clear, logical and compelling — ideal for a well-constructed argument.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Punctuation',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence uses a semicolon correctly to separate items in a list that already contain commas?','{"A":"The committee included delegates from Sydney, NSW; Melbourne, VIC; and Brisbane, QLD.","B":"The committee included delegates from; Sydney NSW; Melbourne VIC; and Brisbane QLD.","C":"The committee included delegates from Sydney NSW, Melbourne VIC, and Brisbane QLD.","D":"The committee included delegates from: Sydney, NSW, Melbourne, VIC, and Brisbane, QLD."}','{"value":"A"}','When list items contain internal commas, semicolons are used between items to avoid confusion.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Voice and Register',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence uses the most appropriate register for a formal report?','{"A":"The results were kind of surprising to everyone.","B":"The results came as a big shock to all involved.","C":"The findings yielded unexpected outcomes across all measured variables.","D":"Nobody expected the results to turn out like that."}','{"value":"C"}','Formal report language is precise, objective and uses technical vocabulary. Option C avoids colloquialisms and subjective language.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Figurative Language',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence uses litotes (understatement via double negative)?','{"A":"He was the best player in the country.","B":"She was not entirely unimpressed by the performance.","C":"The explosion was as quiet as a whisper.","D":"His success was no surprise to anyone."}','{"value":"B"}','Litotes uses a negative statement to affirm the positive: "not entirely unimpressed" = quite impressed.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Tense and Aspect',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence uses the past perfect tense to correctly express priority of events?','{"A":"She left before he arrived.","B":"She had left before he arrived.","C":"She was leaving when he arrived.","D":"She will have left before he arrives."}','{"value":"B"}','The past perfect "had left" clearly establishes that her departure occurred before his arrival.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',9,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Sentence Structure',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which technique does the following sentence use? "It was the best of times, it was the worst of times, it was the age of wisdom, it was the age of foolishness."','{"A":"Asyndeton","B":"Polysyndeton","C":"Anaphora","D":"Chiasmus"}','{"value":"C"}','Anaphora is the repetition of a word or phrase at the beginning of successive clauses: "it was the... it was the..."','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),

